1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,638
Screenshots pile up as Screenshot,

2
00:00:02,638 --> 00:00:06,363
date, time, and nobody can
find the one they need.

3
00:00:06,363 --> 00:00:08,384
Bowerbird is the file mate.

4
00:00:08,384 --> 00:00:13,923
It reads them, proposes honest names,
and moves nothing until you approve.

5
00:00:13,923 --> 00:00:15,258
Bowerbird runs on one PC.

6
00:00:15,258 --> 00:00:21,040
A PowerShell launcher starts the engine,
and your browser talks to it on localhost.

7
00:00:21,740 --> 00:00:26,930
The engine indexes and searches, proposes
renames, and organizes by rules.

8
00:00:26,930 --> 00:00:29,218
The index is encrypted on disk.

9
00:00:29,585 --> 00:00:31,695
Model calls go through Fairlead,

10
00:00:31,695 --> 00:00:34,925
with Bowerbird's own key from
Credential Manager.

11
00:00:34,925 --> 00:00:37,548
The OpenAI key stays in Lazarette.

12
00:00:37,548 --> 00:00:42,051
Semaphore export and SnapShackle
names exist in the code,

13
00:00:42,051 --> 00:00:43,789
but aren't shown here.

14
00:00:44,489 --> 00:00:46,859
One rule holds it together.

15
00:00:46,859 --> 00:00:51,948
Nothing is renamed until you type
APPLY, and a journal can undo it.

16
00:00:52,198 --> 00:00:56,737
The OpenAI key is already in
Lazarette, shared to Fairlead by name.

17
00:00:56,737 --> 00:00:59,421
Fairlead sees only what you share.

18
00:01:00,121 --> 00:01:01,816
Fairlead gives Bowerbird its own key.

19
00:01:01,816 --> 00:01:06,830
Pick Bowerbird, install, and it
lands in Windows Credential Manager.

20
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:12,123
Seven invented screenshots, every
one named Screenshot, date, time.

21
00:01:12,823 --> 00:01:13,852
In Smart Rename, tick AI vision.

22
00:01:14,593 --> 00:01:18,242
Bowerbird asks before any
image leaves this PC.

23
00:01:18,242 --> 00:01:20,813
These are synthetic, so send them.

24
00:01:20,813 --> 00:01:24,951
Seven live vision calls go through
Fairlead to the cloud route,

25
00:01:24,951 --> 00:01:28,104
because Fairlead has no local
vision model here.

26
00:01:28,804 --> 00:01:33,165
Seven proposals, each with its
reason and a confidence.

27
00:01:33,165 --> 00:01:35,124
Nothing has moved yet.

28
00:01:35,824 --> 00:01:37,398
To apply, type APPLY.

29
00:01:37,398 --> 00:01:40,337
The files are renamed exactly
as previewed.

30
00:01:41,037 --> 00:01:42,817
Explorer shows the new names.

31
00:01:43,464 --> 00:01:44,464
Nothing was deleted.

32
00:01:45,149 --> 00:01:46,259
Undo has its own gate.

33
00:01:46,888 --> 00:01:49,089
Type UNDO, and every original
name comes back.

34
00:01:49,339 --> 00:01:50,522
Bowerbird proposes.

35
00:01:50,522 --> 00:01:52,094
People decide.

36
00:01:52,094 --> 00:01:53,704
The names are better,

37
00:01:53,704 --> 00:01:55,620
the moves are reversible,

38
00:01:55,620 --> 00:01:59,299
and the model only ever saw
what you let it see.

39
00:01:59,299 --> 00:02:01,058
That's the watch.
